  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in NAICS 336411 total $33.4B for FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 45.4% year over year while the government awarded 4,358 contracts with an average award size of $7.7M. The Department of Defense accounts for the overwhelming share of buying at $32.9B. Yearly context shows FY26 obligations at $33.4B compared with prior years including $61.2B in FY25 and $60.1B in FY23. The top vendors for FY2026 to date include LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $8.4B and multiple entries for THE BOEING COMPANY totaling several large awards, including $5.8B, $3B, $2.4B, $1.6B, and $1.1B. Other significant vendors are SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION at $2.2B, BELL TEXTRON INC at $1.8B, SIERRA NEVADA COMPANY, LLC at $1.4B, and RTX CORPORATION at $805M. Smaller civilian buyers include the Department of Homeland Security at $136M, Department of Commerce at $108M, and Department of Justice at $101M.",
